e in charge on each shift.","category":"Nursing and Physician Services Deficiencies","concept":"staffing","concept_label":"Staffing & supervision"},"cms-f0803":{"code":"F-0803","title":"Ensure menus must meet the nutritional needs of residents, be prepared in advance, be followed, be updated, be reviewed by dietician, and meet the needs of the resident.","category":"Nutrition and Dietary Deficiencies","concept":"food_nutrition","concept_label":"Food, nutrition & hydration"},"cms-f0804":{"code":"F-0804","title":"Ensure food and drink is palatable, attractive, and at a safe and appetizing temperature.","category":"Nutrition and Dietary Deficiencies","concept":"food_nutrition","concept_label":"Food, nutrition & hydration"},"cms-f0552":{"code":"F-0552","title":"Ensure that residents are fully informed and understand their health status, care and treatments.","category":"Resident Rights Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0684":{"code":"F-0684","title":"Provide appropriate treatment and care according to orders, resident’s preferences and goals.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0689":{"code":"F-0689","title":"Ensure that a nursing home area is free from accident hazards and provides adequate supervision to prevent accidents.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0609":{"code":"F-0609","title":"Timely report suspected abuse, neglect, or theft and report the results of the investigation to proper authorities.","category":"Freedom from Abuse, Neglect, and Exploitation Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0610":{"code":"F-0610","title":"Respond appropriately to all alleged violations.","category":"Freedom from Abuse, Neglect, and Exploitation Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0741":{"code":"F-0741","title":"Ensure that the facility has sufficient staff members who possess the  competencies and skills to meet the behavioral health needs of residents.","category":"Quality of Life and Care Deficiencies","concept":"clinical_care","concept_label":"Clinical care"},"cms-f0607":{"code":"F-0607","title":"Develop and implement policies and procedures to prevent abuse, neglect, and theft.","category":"Freedom from Abuse, Neglect, and Exploitation Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0605":{"code":"F-0605","title":"Prevent the use of unnecessary psychotropic medications or use medications that may restrain a resident's ability to function.","category":"Freedom from Abuse, Neglect, and Exploitation Deficiencies","concept":"resident_rights","concept_label":"Resident rights & abuse/neglect"},"cms-f0730":{"code":"F-0730","title":"Observe each nurse aide's job performance and give regular training.","category":"Nursing and Physician Services Deficiencies","concept":"staffing","concept_label":"Staffing & supervision"},"cms-f0865":{"code":"F-0865","title":"Have a  plan that describes the process for conducting QAPI and QAA activities.","category":"Administration Deficiencies","concept":"administration","concept_label":"Administration & records"},"cms-f0868":{"code":"F-0868","title":"Have the Quality Assessment and Assurance group have the required members and meet at least quarterly","category":"Administration Deficiencies","concept":"administration","concept_label":"Administration & records"},"cms-f0940":{"code":"F-0940","title":"Develop, implement, and/or maintain an effective training program for all new and existing staff members.","category":"Administration Deficiencies","concept":"administration","concept_label":"Administration & records"},"cms-f0947":{"code":"F-0947","title":"Ensure nurse aides have the skills they need to care for resident